module

public import StacksFrontier.Cotangent.StandardResolutionSquare

/-!
# Functoriality of the standard resolution in a square of ring maps

A commutative square of ring maps `A → A'`, `B → B'`, compatible with the algebra structures
`A → B` and `A' → B'` — that is, an object of `CommAlgCat.AlgebraSquare` — induces a *canonical*
map `P_• → P'_•` of the two standard resolutions. It is the one which sends variables to
variables: the standard resolution is the iterated free-forgetful comonad resolution, so its
terms are the iterated polynomial algebras `P_0 = A[B]`, `P_{n+1} = A[P_n]`, and the induced map
maps the coefficients of each layer by `A → A'` and renames its variables by the previous
layer's map. That recursion is the content of `CommAlgCat.standardTowerMap`, and transporting
it along the identification of the terms of the standard resolution with the stages of the
tower gives `CommAlgCat.standardResolutionSquareMap`.

The map so obtained is a map of simplicial rings, is compatible with the two base rings and the
two augmentations, sends variables to variables, and is functorial in the square. These are
exactly the conditions which pin the datum uniquely, so they are the conditions listed by
`CommAlgCat.SquareFunctorialityData`, whose resolution-level fields this file supplies.

## Main definitions

* `CommAlgCat.standardTower`: the `n`-fold iterated polynomial algebra `A[A[⋯[B]⋯]]`, whose
  stage `n + 1` is the degree-`n` term of the standard resolution.
* `CommAlgCat.standardTowerX` and `CommAlgCat.standardResolutionTowerX`: the variable `[q]` of a
  stage of the tower, and of a term of the standard resolution.
* `CommAlgCat.standardTowerFace`, `CommAlgCat.standardTowerDegeneracy`: Godement's faces and
  degeneracies of the polynomial-algebra comonad, read on the tower.
* `CommAlgCat.standardTowerMap`: the variables-to-variables map of towers over a square.
* `CommAlgCat.standardResolutionSquareMap`: the induced map `P_n → P'_n` of standard
  resolutions.

## Main results

* `CommAlgCat.standardResolutionSquareMap_naturality`: it is a map of simplicial rings.
* `CommAlgCat.standardResolutionSquareMap_algebraMap` and
  `CommAlgCat.standardResolutionSquareMap_augmentation_app`: it is compatible with the two base
  rings and with the two augmentations.
* `CommAlgCat.standardResolutionSquareMap_zero_X` and
  `CommAlgCat.standardResolutionSquareMap_succ_X`: it sends variables to variables, in degree
  zero and in every higher degree.
* `CommAlgCat.standardResolutionSquareMap_id` and
  `CommAlgCat.standardResolutionSquareMap_comp`: it is functorial in the square.

## Implementation notes

Naturality is proved only at the faces and the degeneracies and then propagated to every
simplicial operator by `SimplexCategory.morphismProperty_eq_top`, the statement that the
morphisms of the simplex category are generated by them; the propagation is carried by the
multiplicative morphism property `CommAlgCat.standardResolutionSquareMapNaturality`.

The terms of the standard resolution are identified with the stages of the tower by an equality
of algebras which is not a reflexivity, so the comparison maps are `eqToHom` transports
throughout. The faces and degeneracies of the standard resolution are restated through the
tower, with the transports written in terms of
`CommAlgCat.standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower`, so that consecutive transports cancel
syntactically; `CommAlgCat.standardResolution_face` and its companion state the same equations
with transports coming from a different source, against which those cancellations do not fire.

The two base rings are unrelated, so they live in independent universes.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08PM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08PM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08PN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08PN)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite Simplicial

universe u v w

namespace CommAlgCat

/-- The `n`-fold iterated polynomial algebra `A[A[⋯[B]⋯]]`, with `n` pairs of brackets: the value
at `B` of the `n`-fold iterate of the polynomial-algebra comonad. The degree-`n` term of the
standard resolution is the value at `n + 1`. -/
noncomputable def standardTower (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ) :
    CommAlgCat.{max u v} A :=
  ((polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).toFunctor.iterate n).obj B

/-- The zeroth stage of the tower is `B` itself. -/
theorem standardTower_zero (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) :
    standardTower.{u, v} A B 0 = B := rfl

/-- Each stage of the tower is the polynomial algebra on the underlying set of the previous one. -/
theorem standardTower_succ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ) :
    standardTower.{u, v} A B (n + 1) =
      CommAlgCat.of A (MvPolynomial (standardTower.{u, v} A B n) A) := rfl

/-- The degree-`n` term of the standard resolution is the stage `n + 1` of the tower. -/
theorem standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ) :
    (standardResolution.{u, v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋n⦌) = standardTower.{u, v} A B (n + 1) :=
  standardResolution_obj A B n

/-- The variable `[q]` of stage `n + 1` of the tower, indexed by an element `q` of stage `n`. -/
noncomputable def standardTowerX (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ)
    (q : standardTower.{u, v} A B n) : standardTower.{u, v} A B (n + 1) :=
  MvPolynomial.X q

/-- The structure map from the base ring to a stage `n + 1` of the tower is the inclusion of the
constant polynomials. -/
theorem standardTower_algebraMap_succ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A)
    (n : ℕ) (a : A) :
    algebraMap A (standardTower.{u, v} A B (n + 1)) a =
      (MvPolynomial.C a : MvPolynomial (standardTower.{u, v} A B n) A) :=
  MvPolynomial.algebraMap_eq (R := A) (σ := standardTower.{u, v} A B n) ▸ rfl

/-- Two ring homomorphisms out of the stage `n + 1` of the tower agree as soon as they agree on
the image of the base ring and on the variables. -/
theorem standardTower_succ_hom_ext (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ)
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {f g : standardTower.{u, v} A B (n + 1) →+* R}
    (hC : ∀ a : A, f (algebraMap A (standardTower.{u, v} A B (n + 1)) a) =
      g (algebraMap A (standardTower.{u, v} A B (n + 1)) a))
    (hX : ∀ q : standardTower.{u, v} A B n,
      f (standardTowerX.{u, v} A B n q) = g (standardTowerX.{u, v} A B n q)) :
    f = g :=
  MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext hC hX

/-- The polynomial algebra functor on a square of a ring map and a map of variable sets: the
coefficients are mapped by `f` and the variables renamed by `g`. -/
noncomputable def mvPolynomialMapRename {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {A' : Type w} [CommRing A']
    (f : A →+* A') {σ : Type*} {σ' : Type*} (g : σ → σ') :
    MvPolynomial σ A →+* MvPolynomial σ' A' :=
  (MvPolynomial.rename g).toRingHom.comp (MvPolynomial.map f)

/-- `mvPolynomialMapRename` on a constant polynomial. -/
@[simp]
theorem mvPolynomialMapRename_C {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {A' : Type w} [CommRing A']
    (f : A →+* A') {σ σ' : Type*} (g : σ → σ') (a : A) :
    mvPolynomialMapRename f g (MvPolynomial.C a) = MvPolynomial.C (f a) := by
  simp [mvPolynomialMapRename]

/-- `mvPolynomialMapRename` on a variable. -/
@[simp]
theorem mvPolynomialMapRename_X {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {A' : Type w} [CommRing A']
    (f : A →+* A') {σ σ' : Type*} (g : σ → σ') (s : σ) :
    mvPolynomialMapRename f g (MvPolynomial.X s) = MvPolynomial.X (g s) := by
  simp [mvPolynomialMapRename]

/-- A morphism of commutative algebras applied through its underlying ring homomorphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem hom_toRingHom_apply {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {X Y : CommAlgCat.{v} A} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (x : X) : f.hom.toRingHom x = f x := rfl

/-- The polynomial-algebra comonad renames variables: its value on a map `f` sends the variable
`[c]` to the variable `[f c]`. -/
theorem polynomialComonad_map_X (A : Type u) [CommRing A] {C D : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A}
    (f : C ⟶ D) (c : C) :
    ((polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).toFunctor.map f) (MvPolynomial.X c) =
      MvPolynomial.X (f c) :=
  MvPolynomial.rename_X (f := ⇑f) c

/-- The polynomial-algebra comonad sends the variable `[q]` of a stage of the tower to the
variable `[f q]`. -/
theorem polynomialComonad_map_standardTowerX (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) {m n : ℕ}
    (f : standardTower.{u, v} A B n ⟶ standardTower.{u, v} A B m)
    (q : standardTower.{u, v} A B n) :
    (polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).toFunctor.map f (standardTowerX.{u, v} A B n q) =
      standardTowerX.{u, v} A B m (f q) :=
  polynomialComonad_map_X A f q

/-- The `j`-th face of Godement's standard resolution of the polynomial-algebra comonad, read on
the tower of iterated polynomial algebras. -/
noncomputable def standardTowerFace (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ)
    (j : Fin (n + 1)) : standardTower.{u, v} A B (n + 1) ⟶ standardTower.{u, v} A B n :=
  (Godement.face (polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).ε n j).app B

/-- The `j`-th degeneracy of Godement's standard resolution of the polynomial-algebra comonad,
read on the tower of iterated polynomial algebras. -/
noncomputable def standardTowerDegeneracy (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ) (j : Fin (n + 1)) :
    standardTower.{u, v} A B (n + 1) ⟶ standardTower.{u, v} A B (n + 2) :=
  (Godement.degeneracy (polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).δ n j).app B

/-- The zeroth face is the counit of the polynomial-algebra comonad at the previous stage. -/
theorem standardTowerFace_zero (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ) :
    standardTowerFace.{u, v} A B n 0 =
      (polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).ε.app (standardTower.{u, v} A B n) :=
  NatTrans.congr_app (Godement.Prep.face_zero (polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).ε n) B

/-- Every higher face is the previous one renamed into the outermost layer of variables. -/
theorem standardTowerFace_succ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ)
    (j : Fin (n + 1)) :
    standardTowerFace.{u, v} A B (n + 1) j.succ =
      (polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).toFunctor.map (standardTowerFace.{u, v} A B n j) :=
  NatTrans.congr_app (Godement.Prep.face_succ (polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).ε n j) B

/-- The zeroth degeneracy is the comultiplication of the polynomial-algebra comonad at the
previous stage. -/
theorem standardTowerDegeneracy_zero (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A)
    (n : ℕ) :
    standardTowerDegeneracy.{u, v} A B n 0 =
      (polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).δ.app (standardTower.{u, v} A B n) :=
  NatTrans.congr_app (Godement.Prep.degeneracy_zero (polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).δ n) B

/-- Every higher degeneracy is the previous one renamed into the outermost layer of variables. -/
theorem standardTowerDegeneracy_succ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ)
    (j : Fin (n + 1)) :
    standardTowerDegeneracy.{u, v} A B (n + 1) j.succ =
      (polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).toFunctor.map (standardTowerDegeneracy.{u, v} A B n j) :=
  NatTrans.congr_app (Godement.Prep.degeneracy_succ (polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).δ n j) B

/-- The zeroth face deletes the outermost layer of brackets: it sends the variable `[q]` to `q`. -/
@[simp]
theorem standardTowerFace_zero_standardTowerX (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A)
    (n : ℕ) (q : standardTower.{u, v} A B n) :
    standardTowerFace.{u, v} A B n 0 (standardTowerX.{u, v} A B n q) = q := by
  rw [standardTowerFace_zero]
  show ((polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).ε.app
    (standardTower.{u, v} A B n)).hom (MvPolynomial.X q) = q
  rw [polynomialComonad_counit]
  exact MvPolynomial.aeval_X (id : standardTower.{u, v} A B n → _) q

/-- The zeroth degeneracy doubles the outermost layer of brackets: it sends the variable `[q]` to
the variable `[[q]]`. -/
@[simp]
theorem standardTowerDegeneracy_zero_standardTowerX (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ) (q : standardTower.{u, v} A B n) :
    standardTowerDegeneracy.{u, v} A B n 0 (standardTowerX.{u, v} A B n q) =
      standardTowerX.{u, v} A B (n + 1) (standardTowerX.{u, v} A B n q) := by
  rw [standardTowerDegeneracy_zero]
  show ((polynomialComonad.{u, v} A).δ.app
    (standardTower.{u, v} A B n)).hom (MvPolynomial.X q) = _
  rw [polynomialComonad_comul]
  exact MvPolynomial.rename_X (f := (MvPolynomial.X : standardTower.{u, v} A B n → _)) q

/-- The faces of the standard resolution, read through the identification of its terms with the
stages of the tower of iterated polynomial algebras. -/
theorem standardResolution_delta_apply (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A)
    (n : ℕ) (j : Fin (n + 2)) (p : (standardResolution.{u, v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋n + 1⦌)) :
    (standardResolution.{u, v} A B).left.δ j p =
      eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, v} A B n).symm
        (standardTowerFace.{u, v} A B (n + 1) j
          (eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, v} A B (n + 1)) p)) :=
  ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (standardResolution_face.{u, v} A B n j) p

/-- The degeneracies of the standard resolution, read through the identification of its terms
with the stages of the tower of iterated polynomial algebras. -/
theorem standardResolution_sigma_apply (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A)
    (n : ℕ) (j : Fin (n + 1)) (p : (standardResolution.{u, v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋n⦌)) :
    (standardResolution.{u, v} A B).left.σ j p =
      eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, v} A B (n + 1)).symm
        (standardTowerDegeneracy.{u, v} A B n j
          (eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, v} A B n) p)) :=
  ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (standardResolution_degeneracy.{u, v} A B n j) p

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {A' : Type w} [CommRing A']
  {B : CommAlgCat.{max u w v} A} {B' : CommAlgCat.{max u w v} A'}

/-- The map of iterated polynomial algebras induced by a commutative square of ring maps: in
degree zero it is `sq.map`, and each further layer maps the coefficients by `sq.base` and renames
the variables by the previous layer's map. This is the recursion "variables go to variables" which
makes the functoriality of the standard resolution canonical. -/
noncomputable def standardTowerMap (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') :
    (n : ℕ) → (standardTower.{u, max w v} A B n →+* standardTower.{w, max u v} A' B' n)
  | 0 => sq.map
  | n + 1 => mvPolynomialMapRename sq.base ⇑(standardTowerMap sq n)

/-- In degree zero the tower map is the given map of algebras. -/
theorem standardTowerMap_zero (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') :
    standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq 0 = sq.map := rfl

/-- The tower map sends the variable `[q]` to the variable `[u q]`. -/
@[simp]
theorem standardTowerMap_standardTowerX (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') (n : ℕ)
    (q : standardTower.{u, max w v} A B n) :
    standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n + 1) (standardTowerX.{u, max w v} A B n q) =
      standardTowerX.{w, max u v} A' B' n (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq n q) :=
  mvPolynomialMapRename_X sq.base _ q

/-- The tower map is compatible with the structure maps from the two base rings. -/
theorem standardTowerMap_algebraMap (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') (n : ℕ) (a : A) :
    standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq n (algebraMap A (standardTower.{u, max w v} A B n) a) =
      algebraMap A' (standardTower.{w, max u v} A' B' n) (sq.base a) := by
  cases n with
  | zero => exact sq.map_algebraMap a
  | succ n =>
      rw [standardTower_algebraMap_succ, standardTower_algebraMap_succ]
      exact mvPolynomialMapRename_C sq.base _ a

/-- The two sides of a commutation statement for the tower map agree on the image of the base
ring, for any pair of algebra maps out of consecutive stages over the square. -/
theorem standardTowerMap_commutes_algebraMap (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') {m n : ℕ}
    (f : standardTower.{u, max w v} A B (n + 1) ⟶ standardTower.{u, max w v} A B m)
    (f' : standardTower.{w, max u v} A' B' (n + 1) ⟶ standardTower.{w, max u v} A' B' m)
    (a : A) :
    standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq m (f (algebraMap A (standardTower.{u, max w v} A B (n + 1)) a)) =
      f' (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n + 1)
        (algebraMap A (standardTower.{u, max w v} A B (n + 1)) a)) := by
  rw [f.hom.commutes a, standardTowerMap_algebraMap, standardTowerMap_algebraMap, f'.hom.commutes]

/-- A pair of maps out of consecutive stages over the square commutes with the tower map as soon
as it does so on the variables of the outermost layer. -/
private theorem standardTowerMap_commutes_of_X (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') {m n : ℕ}
    (f : standardTower.{u, max w v} A B (n + 1) ⟶ standardTower.{u, max w v} A B m)
    (f' : standardTower.{w, max u v} A' B' (n + 1) ⟶ standardTower.{w, max u v} A' B' m)
    (hX : ∀ q : standardTower.{u, max w v} A B n,
      standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq m (f (standardTowerX.{u, max w v} A B n q)) =
        f' (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n + 1) (standardTowerX.{u, max w v} A B n q)))
    (p : standardTower.{u, max w v} A B (n + 1)) :
    standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq m (f p) = f' (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n + 1) p) :=
  DFunLike.congr_fun (standardTower_succ_hom_ext.{u, max w v} A B n
    (f := (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq m).comp f.hom.toRingHom)
    (g := f'.hom.toRingHom.comp (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n + 1)))
    (fun a => by
      simpa only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, hom_toRingHom_apply] using
        standardTowerMap_commutes_algebraMap sq f f' a) hX) p

/-- The inductive step of the commutation proofs: a pair of maps of stages which commutes with
the tower map stays commuting after being renamed into the outermost layer of variables. -/
theorem standardTowerMap_polynomialComonad_map (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') {m n : ℕ}
    (f : standardTower.{u, max w v} A B n ⟶ standardTower.{u, max w v} A B m)
    (f' : standardTower.{w, max u v} A' B' n ⟶ standardTower.{w, max u v} A' B' m)
    (hf : ∀ q, standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq m (f q) = f' (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq n q))
    (p : standardTower.{u, max w v} A B (n + 1)) :
    standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (m + 1) ((polynomialComonad.{u, max w v} A).toFunctor.map f p) =
      (polynomialComonad.{w, max u v} A').toFunctor.map f'
        (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n + 1) p) :=
  standardTowerMap_commutes_of_X sq (m := m + 1) (n := n)
    ((polynomialComonad.{u, max w v} A).toFunctor.map f)
    ((polynomialComonad.{w, max u v} A').toFunctor.map f') (fun q => by
    change standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (m + 1) ((polynomialComonad.{u, max w v} A).toFunctor.map f
        (standardTowerX.{u, max w v} A B n q)) =
      (polynomialComonad.{w, max u v} A').toFunctor.map f'
        (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n + 1) (standardTowerX.{u, max w v} A B n q))
    rw [polynomialComonad_map_standardTowerX, standardTowerMap_standardTowerX,
      standardTowerMap_standardTowerX, polynomialComonad_map_standardTowerX, hf]) p

/-- The tower map commutes with the zeroth face in every degree: both sides evaluate the
outermost layer of variables. -/
theorem standardTowerMap_face_zero (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') (n : ℕ)
    (p : standardTower.{u, max w v} A B (n + 1)) :
    standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq n (standardTowerFace.{u, max w v} A B n 0 p) =
      standardTowerFace.{w, max u v} A' B' n 0 (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n + 1) p) :=
  standardTowerMap_commutes_of_X sq _ _ (fun q => by
    simp only [standardTowerFace_zero_standardTowerX, standardTowerMap_standardTowerX]) p

/-- The tower map commutes with every face of the standard resolution. -/
theorem standardTowerMap_face (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') (n : ℕ) :
    ∀ (j : Fin (n + 1)) (p : standardTower.{u, max w v} A B (n + 1)),
      standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq n (standardTowerFace.{u, max w v} A B n j p) =
        standardTowerFace.{w, max u v} A' B' n j (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n + 1) p) := by
  induction n with
  | zero =>
      intro j p
      induction j using Fin.cases with
      | zero => exact standardTowerMap_face_zero sq 0 p
      | succ i => exact i.elim0
  | succ n ih =>
      intro j p
      induction j using Fin.cases with
      | zero => exact standardTowerMap_face_zero sq (n + 1) p
      | succ i =>
          rw [standardTowerFace_succ, standardTowerFace_succ]
          exact standardTowerMap_polynomialComonad_map sq (standardTowerFace.{u, max w v} A B n i)
            (standardTowerFace.{w, max u v} A' B' n i) (ih i) p

/-- The tower map commutes with the zeroth degeneracy in every degree: both sides double the
outermost layer of brackets. -/
theorem standardTowerMap_degeneracy_zero (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') (n : ℕ)
    (p : standardTower.{u, max w v} A B (n + 1)) :
    standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n + 2) (standardTowerDegeneracy.{u, max w v} A B n 0 p) =
      standardTowerDegeneracy.{w, max u v} A' B' n 0 (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n + 1) p) :=
  standardTowerMap_commutes_of_X sq _ _ (fun q => by
    simp only [standardTowerDegeneracy_zero_standardTowerX, standardTowerMap_standardTowerX]) p

/-- The tower map commutes with every degeneracy of the standard resolution. -/
theorem standardTowerMap_degeneracy (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') (n : ℕ) :
    ∀ (j : Fin (n + 1)) (p : standardTower.{u, max w v} A B (n + 1)),
      standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n + 2) (standardTowerDegeneracy.{u, max w v} A B n j p) =
        standardTowerDegeneracy.{w, max u v} A' B' n j
          (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n + 1) p) := by
  induction n with
  | zero =>
      intro j p
      induction j using Fin.cases with
      | zero => exact standardTowerMap_degeneracy_zero sq 0 p
      | succ i => exact i.elim0
  | succ n ih =>
      intro j p
      induction j using Fin.cases with
      | zero => exact standardTowerMap_degeneracy_zero sq (n + 1) p
      | succ i =>
          rw [standardTowerDegeneracy_succ, standardTowerDegeneracy_succ]
          exact standardTowerMap_polynomialComonad_map sq
            (standardTowerDegeneracy.{u, max w v} A B n i)
            (standardTowerDegeneracy.{w, max u v} A' B' n i) (ih i) p

/-! ### The induced map of standard resolutions -/

/-- Transporting an element along two equalities of algebras with matching endpoints returns it.
Unlike `CommAlgCat.eqToHom_eqToHom_symm_apply` the two proofs are unrelated, so this rewrites
against transports whose proofs came from different sources. -/
theorem eqToHom_eqToHom_apply {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {X Y : CommAlgCat.{v} R} (h : X = Y)
    (h' : Y = X) (x : X) : eqToHom h' (eqToHom h x) = x := by
  rw [← CommAlgCat.comp_apply, eqToHom_trans, eqToHom_refl, CommAlgCat.id_apply]

/-- The map `P_n → P'_n` of standard resolutions induced by a commutative square of ring maps:
the tower map of the corresponding stage, transported along the identification of the degree-`n`
term of the standard resolution with that stage. -/
noncomputable def standardResolutionSquareMap (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B')
    (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    (standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.obj n →+*
      (standardResolution.{w, max u v} A' B').left.obj n :=
  ((eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{w, max u v} A' B'
        n.unop.len).symm).hom.toRingHom.comp
    (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (n.unop.len + 1))).comp
      (eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, max w v} A B
        n.unop.len)).hom.toRingHom

/-- In degree `n` the induced map of standard resolutions is the stage-`n + 1` tower map read
through the identification of the term with the stage. -/
theorem standardResolutionSquareMap_apply (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') (k : ℕ)
    (p : (standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋k⦌)) :
    standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋k⦌) p =
      eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{w, max u v} A' B' k).symm
        (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq (k + 1)
          (eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, max w v} A B k) p)) := rfl

/-- The induced map of standard resolutions is compatible with the structure maps from the two
base rings. -/
theorem standardResolutionSquareMap_algebraMap (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B')
    (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) (a : A) :
    standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq n
        (algebraMap A ((standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.obj n) a) =
      algebraMap A' ((standardResolution.{w, max u v} A' B').left.obj n) (sq.base a) := by
  rw [standardResolutionSquareMap_apply sq n.unop.len,
    (eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, max w v} A B
      n.unop.len)).hom.commutes a, standardTowerMap_algebraMap,
    (eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{w, max u v} A' B'
      n.unop.len).symm).hom.commutes]

/-- The naturality square of the induced map of standard resolutions at a morphism of the simplex
category: the property whose multiplicativity and validity at the faces and the degeneracies
yield naturality at every simplicial operator. -/
noncomputable def standardResolutionSquareMapNaturality
    (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') : MorphismProperty SimplexCategory :=
  fun x y φ => ∀ p : (standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.obj (op y),
    standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op x)
        ((standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.map φ.op p) =
      (standardResolution.{w, max u v} A' B').left.map φ.op
        (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op y) p)

/-- The naturality property of the induced map of standard resolutions is closed under identities
and composition. -/
instance standardResolutionSquareMapNaturality_isMultiplicative
    (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') :
    (standardResolutionSquareMapNaturality.{u, v, w} sq).IsMultiplicative where
  id_mem x := by
    intro p
    simp only [op_id, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id, CommAlgCat.id_apply]
  comp_mem {x y z} φ ψ hφ hψ := by
    intro p
    have h : (standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.map (φ ≫ ψ).op p =
        (standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.map φ.op
          ((standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.map ψ.op p) := by
      rw [op_comp, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp, CommAlgCat.comp_apply]
    have h' : (standardResolution.{w, max u v} A' B').left.map (φ ≫ ψ).op
          (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op z) p) =
        (standardResolution.{w, max u v} A' B').left.map φ.op
          ((standardResolution.{w, max u v} A' B').left.map ψ.op
            (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op z) p)) := by
      rw [op_comp, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp, CommAlgCat.comp_apply]
    rw [h, h', hφ, hψ p]

/-- The induced map of standard resolutions commutes with every face. -/
theorem standardResolutionSquareMap_δ (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') (n : ℕ)
    (j : Fin (n + 2)) (p : (standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋n + 1⦌)) :
    standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋n⦌)
        ((standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.δ j p) =
      (standardResolution.{w, max u v} A' B').left.δ j
        (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋n + 1⦌) p) := by
  rw [standardResolution_delta_apply.{u, max w v} A B n j p,
    standardResolution_delta_apply.{w, max u v} A' B' n j
      (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋n + 1⦌) p),
    standardResolutionSquareMap_apply, standardResolutionSquareMap_apply,
    eqToHom_eqToHom_apply, eqToHom_eqToHom_apply]
  exact congrArg _ (standardTowerMap_face sq (n + 1) j _)

/-- The induced map of standard resolutions commutes with every degeneracy. -/
theorem standardResolutionSquareMap_σ (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') (n : ℕ)
    (j : Fin (n + 1)) (p : (standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋n⦌)) :
    standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋n + 1⦌)
        ((standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.σ j p) =
      (standardResolution.{w, max u v} A' B').left.σ j
        (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋n⦌) p) := by
  rw [standardResolution_sigma_apply.{u, max w v} A B n j p,
    standardResolution_sigma_apply.{w, max u v} A' B' n j
      (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋n⦌) p),
    standardResolutionSquareMap_apply, standardResolutionSquareMap_apply,
    eqToHom_eqToHom_apply, eqToHom_eqToHom_apply]
  exact congrArg _ (standardTowerMap_degeneracy sq n j _)

/-- The induced map of standard resolutions is a map of simplicial rings: it commutes with every
simplicial operator. -/
theorem standardResolutionSquareMap_naturality (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B')
    {i j : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ} (g : i ⟶ j)
    (p : (standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.obj i) :
    standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq j
        ((standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.map g p) =
      (standardResolution.{w, max u v} A' B').left.map g
        (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq i p) := by
  have htop : standardResolutionSquareMapNaturality.{u, v, w} sq = ⊤ :=
    SimplexCategory.morphismProperty_eq_top _
      (fun {n} i => standardResolutionSquareMap_δ sq n i)
      (fun {n} i => standardResolutionSquareMap_σ sq n i)
  have h : standardResolutionSquareMapNaturality.{u, v, w} sq g.unop := by
    rw [htop]
    trivial
  exact h p

/-! ### The variables, the augmentations, and functoriality in the square -/

/-- The variable `[q]` of the degree-`n` term of the standard resolution, indexed by an element
of the stage-`n` tower. -/
noncomputable def standardResolutionTowerX (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ) (q : standardTower.{u, v} A B n) :
    (standardResolution.{u, v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋n⦌) :=
  eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, v} A B n).symm
    (standardTowerX.{u, v} A B n q)

/-- Two ring homomorphisms out of the degree-`n` term of the standard resolution agree as soon as
they agree on the image of the base ring and on the variables. -/
theorem standardResolution_obj_hom_ext (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A)
    (n : ℕ) {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    {f g : (standardResolution.{u, v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋n⦌) →+* R}
    (hC : ∀ a : A, f (algebraMap A ((standardResolution.{u, v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋n⦌)) a) =
      g (algebraMap A ((standardResolution.{u, v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋n⦌)) a))
    (hX : ∀ q : standardTower.{u, v} A B n,
      f (standardResolutionTowerX.{u, v} A B n q) =
        g (standardResolutionTowerX.{u, v} A B n q)) :
    f = g := by
  have hcom := (eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, v} A B n).symm).hom.commutes
  have key : f.comp
        (eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, v} A B n).symm).hom.toRingHom =
      g.comp
        (eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, v} A B n).symm).hom.toRingHom :=
    standardTower_succ_hom_ext.{u, v} A B n
      (fun a => ((congrArg (⇑f) (hcom a)).trans ((hC a).trans
        (congrArg (⇑g) (hcom a)).symm)))
      (fun q => hX q)
  refine RingHom.ext fun x => ?_
  have hx := DFunLike.congr_fun key
    (eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, v} A B n) x)
  simpa only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, hom_toRingHom_apply,
    eqToHom_eqToHom_apply] using hx

/-- The induced map of standard resolutions sends the variable `[q]` to the variable `[u q]`,
where `u` is the tower map of the previous stage. -/
theorem standardResolutionSquareMap_standardResolutionTowerX
    (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') (n : ℕ)
    (q : standardTower.{u, max w v} A B n) :
    standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋n⦌)
        (standardResolutionTowerX.{u, max w v} A B n q) =
      standardResolutionTowerX.{w, max u v} A' B' n (standardTowerMap.{u, v, w} sq n q) := by
  rw [standardResolutionTowerX, standardResolutionSquareMap_apply, eqToHom_eqToHom_apply,
    standardTowerMap_standardTowerX, standardResolutionTowerX]

/-- The augmentation of the standard resolution is compatible with the structure map from the
base ring. -/
theorem standardResolutionAugmentationHom_algebraMap (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) (a : A) :
    standardResolutionAugmentationHom.{u, v} A B n
        (algebraMap A ((standardResolution.{u, v} A B).left.obj n) a) = algebraMap A B a :=
  ((standardResolution.{u, v} A B).hom.app n).hom.commutes a

/-- In degree zero the augmentation sends the variable `[b]` to `b`. -/
theorem standardResolutionAugmentationHom_standardResolutionTowerX_zero (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (b : standardTower.{u, v} A B 0) :
    standardResolutionAugmentationHom.{u, v} A B (op ⦋0⦌)
        (standardResolutionTowerX.{u, v} A B 0 b) = b :=
  standardResolution_augmentation_X A B b

/-- The augmentation in degree `n + 1` is the augmentation in degree `n` after the zeroth
face. -/
theorem standardResolutionAugmentationHom_delta_zero (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ)
    (p : (standardResolution.{u, v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋n + 1⦌)) :
    standardResolutionAugmentationHom.{u, v} A B (op ⦋n⦌)
        ((standardResolution.{u, v} A B).left.δ (0 : Fin (n + 2)) p) =
      standardResolutionAugmentationHom.{u, v} A B (op ⦋n + 1⦌) p :=
  DFunLike.congr_fun (standardResolutionAugmentationHom_naturality.{u, v} A B
    (SimplexCategory.δ (0 : Fin (n + 2))).op) p

/-- The induced map of standard resolutions is compatible with the two augmentations. -/
theorem standardResolutionSquareMap_augmentation (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B')
    (n : ℕ) : ∀ p : (standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋n⦌),
      standardResolutionAugmentationHom.{w, max u v} A' B' (op ⦋n⦌)
          (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋n⦌) p) =
        sq.map (standardResolutionAugmentationHom.{u, max w v} A B (op ⦋n⦌) p) := by
  induction n with
  | zero =>
      intro p
      refine DFunLike.congr_fun (standardResolution_obj_hom_ext.{u, max w v} A B 0
        (f := (standardResolutionAugmentationHom.{w, max u v} A' B' (op ⦋0⦌)).comp
          (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋0⦌)))
        (g := sq.map.comp (standardResolutionAugmentationHom.{u, max w v} A B (op ⦋0⦌)))
        (fun a => ?_) (fun b => ?_)) p
      · simp only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply,
          standardResolutionSquareMap_algebraMap,
          standardResolutionAugmentationHom_algebraMap, sq.map_algebraMap]
      · simp only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply,
          standardResolutionSquareMap_standardResolutionTowerX,
          standardResolutionAugmentationHom_standardResolutionTowerX_zero, standardTowerMap_zero]
        rfl
  | succ n ih =>
      intro p
      rw [← standardResolutionAugmentationHom_delta_zero.{w, max u v} A' B' n
          (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋n + 1⦌) p),
        ← standardResolutionAugmentationHom_delta_zero.{u, max w v} A B n p,
        ← standardResolutionSquareMap_δ sq n 0 p, ih]

/-- The induced map of standard resolutions is compatible with the two augmentations, in every
simplicial degree. -/
theorem standardResolutionSquareMap_augmentation_app (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B')
    (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) (p : (standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.obj n) :
    standardResolutionAugmentationHom.{w, max u v} A' B' n
        (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq n p) =
      sq.map (standardResolutionAugmentationHom.{u, max w v} A B n p) :=
  standardResolutionSquareMap_augmentation sq n.unop.len p

/-- The two readings of a variable of a polynomial algebra whose index algebra is presented in
two ways: transporting the index and transporting the whole algebra give the same variable. -/
theorem eqToHom_mvPolynomial_X {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {P Q S : CommAlgCat.{max u v} R}
    (hPQ : P = Q)
    (hSP : S = CommAlgCat.of R (MvPolynomial P R))
    (hSQ : S = CommAlgCat.of R (MvPolynomial Q R)) (x : P) :
    eqToHom hSP.symm (MvPolynomial.X x : CommAlgCat.of R (MvPolynomial P R)) =
      eqToHom hSQ.symm
        (MvPolynomial.X (eqToHom hPQ x) : CommAlgCat.of R (MvPolynomial Q R)) := by
  subst hPQ
  rw [eqToHom_refl, CommAlgCat.id_apply]

/-- In degree zero the variable of the standard resolution indexed by `b` is the variable `[b]`
of the polynomial algebra `A[B]`. -/
theorem standardResolutionTowerX_zero (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A)
    (b : B) :
    standardResolutionTowerX.{u, v} A B 0 b =
      (standardResolutionZeroAlgEquiv.{u, v} A B).symm (MvPolynomial.X b) := rfl

/-- The variable of the degree-`n + 1` term of the standard resolution, read through the tower. -/
theorem standardResolutionX_eq_standardResolutionTowerX (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ)
    (q : (standardResolution.{u, v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋n⦌)) :
    standardResolutionX.{u, v} A B n q =
      standardResolutionTowerX.{u, v} A B (n + 1)
        (eqToHom (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, v} A B n) q) :=
  eqToHom_mvPolynomial_X (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, v} A B n)
    (standardResolution_obj_succ.{u, v} A B n)
    (standardResolution_obj_eq_standardTower.{u, v} A B (n + 1)) q

/-- **Variables go to variables, in degree zero.** The induced map of standard resolutions sends
the variable `[b]` of `P₀ = A[B]` to the variable `[sq.map b]` of `P'₀ = A'[B']`. This is the
`resolution_zero_X` field of `CommAlgCat.SquareFunctorialityData`. -/
theorem standardResolutionSquareMap_zero_X (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') (b : B) :
    standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋0⦌)
        ((standardResolutionZeroAlgEquiv.{u, max w v} A B).symm (MvPolynomial.X b)) =
      (standardResolutionZeroAlgEquiv.{w, max u v} A' B').symm
        (MvPolynomial.X (sq.map b)) :=
  standardResolutionSquareMap_standardResolutionTowerX sq 0 b

/-- **Variables go to variables, in every higher degree.** The induced map of standard
resolutions sends the variable `[q]` of `P_{n+1} = A[P_n]` to the variable `[u q]` of
`P'_{n+1} = A'[P'_n]`, where `u` is the degree-`n` map. This is the `resolution_succ_X` field of
`CommAlgCat.SquareFunctorialityData`. -/
theorem standardResolutionSquareMap_succ_X (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, w} A A' B B') (n : ℕ)
    (q : (standardResolution.{u, max w v} A B).left.obj (op ⦋n⦌)) :
    standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋n + 1⦌)
        (standardResolutionX.{u, max w v} A B n q) =
      standardResolutionX.{w, max u v} A' B' n
        (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, w} sq (op ⦋n⦌) q) := by
  rw [standardResolutionX_eq_standardResolutionTowerX,
    standardResolutionSquareMap_standardResolutionTowerX,
    standardResolutionX_eq_standardResolutionTowerX, standardResolutionSquareMap_apply,
    eqToHom_eqToHom_apply]

/-- The tower map of an identity square is the identity. -/
theorem standardTowerMap_id (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A) (n : ℕ) :
    standardTowerMap.{u, v, u} (AlgebraSquare.id.{u, v} A B) n =
      RingHom.id (standardTower.{u, max u v} A B n) := by
  induction n with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ n ih =>
      refine standardTower_succ_hom_ext.{u, max u v} A B n (fun a => ?_) (fun q => ?_)
      · rw [standardTowerMap_algebraMap]
        rfl
      · rw [standardTowerMap_standardTowerX, ih]
        rfl

/-- The tower map of a composition of squares is the composition of the tower maps. -/
theorem standardTowerMap_comp {A A' A'' : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing A'] [CommRing A'']
    {B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A} {B' : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A'} {B'' : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A''}
    (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, u} A A' B B') (sq' : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, u} A' A'' B' B'')
    (n : ℕ) :
    standardTowerMap.{u, v, u} (sq.comp sq') n =
      (standardTowerMap.{u, v, u} sq' n).comp (standardTowerMap.{u, v, u} sq n) := by
  induction n with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ n ih =>
      refine standardTower_succ_hom_ext.{u, max u v} A B n (fun a => ?_) (fun q => ?_)
      · rw [standardTowerMap_algebraMap, RingHom.comp_apply, standardTowerMap_algebraMap,
          standardTowerMap_algebraMap]
        rfl
      · rw [standardTowerMap_standardTowerX, RingHom.comp_apply, standardTowerMap_standardTowerX,
          standardTowerMap_standardTowerX, ih]
        rfl

/-- The functoriality of the standard resolution is natural in squares: an identity square
induces the identity map of standard resolutions. -/
theorem standardResolutionSquareMap_id (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A)
    (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, u} (AlgebraSquare.id.{u, v} A B) n =
      RingHom.id ((standardResolution.{u, max u v} A B).left.obj n) := by
  refine RingHom.ext fun p => ?_
  rw [standardResolutionSquareMap_apply, standardTowerMap_id, RingHom.id_apply,
    eqToHom_eqToHom_apply, RingHom.id_apply]

/-- The functoriality of the standard resolution is natural in squares: a composition of squares
induces the composition of the maps of standard resolutions. -/
theorem standardResolutionSquareMap_comp {A A' A'' : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing A']
    [CommRing A''] {B : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A} {B' : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A'}
    {B'' : CommAlgCat.{max u v} A''} (sq : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, u} A A' B B')
    (sq' : AlgebraSquare.{u, v, u} A' A'' B' B'') (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, u} (sq.comp sq') n =
      (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, u} sq' n).comp
        (standardResolutionSquareMap.{u, v, u} sq n) := by
  refine RingHom.ext fun p => ?_
  rw [standardResolutionSquareMap_apply, standardTowerMap_comp, RingHom.comp_apply,
    RingHom.comp_apply, standardResolutionSquareMap_apply, standardResolutionSquareMap_apply,
    eqToHom_eqToHom_apply]

end CommAlgCat

